WEBVTT

00:04.480 --> 00:08.010
So this is the sea of Irago...

00:09.170 --> 00:14.370
And that's the penal colony where
Omi no Okimi was once exiled!

00:15.550 --> 00:16.950
Waves crash

00:16.950 --> 00:19.770
as I lament how fleeting life is

00:19.770 --> 00:21.290
and feast on the island seaweed

00:21.290 --> 00:22.800
from Irago Island.

00:25.170 --> 00:27.620
We're standing in the very spot

00:27.620 --> 00:29.710
where he composed that poem!

00:29.710 --> 00:31.920
My heart's going to burst!

00:32.620 --> 00:36.130
I didn't expect Komachi
to get so excited.

00:36.130 --> 00:40.030
Well, most poets are also fans.

00:40.030 --> 00:42.520
They're dying to visit the original sites.

00:42.890 --> 00:45.350
It's like a sacred pilgrimage to them.

00:46.160 --> 00:47.060
Where's Mount Fuji?

00:47.290 --> 00:49.960
That's the one Yamabe
no Akahito spoke of!

00:51.300 --> 00:53.430
Mount Fuji is more to the east.

00:53.430 --> 00:56.070
Really?  I can't wait to see it!

00:56.950 --> 00:58.310
Once Mount Fuji is within sight,

00:58.310 --> 01:00.760
the three of us can
recite poems together!

01:01.200 --> 01:03.550
Recite the poem Akahito composed

01:03.550 --> 01:05.220
as he gazed at Mount Fuji!

01:06.650 --> 01:08.640
That will be lovely!

01:09.270 --> 01:10.460
Fangirl...

01:12.070 --> 01:15.300
Are you wondering why we're here?

02:53.310 --> 02:54.400
Yoshiko-sama.

02:55.740 --> 02:58.530
You have a letter from Yasuhide-sama.

02:59.010 --> 03:00.300
Thank you.

03:00.300 --> 03:02.110
Perhaps he wishes you a happy new year?

03:02.430 --> 03:03.590
Most likely.

03:04.050 --> 03:05.910
He is a diligent man.

03:06.990 --> 03:10.250
We first met when I was still a servant.

03:11.480 --> 03:14.460
Yasuhide-sama, Narihira-sama,
and myself...

03:14.830 --> 03:17.020
We chatted and gazed
at the moon together.

03:17.850 --> 03:20.270
Ever since, we have exchanged
letters from time to time.

03:21.880 --> 03:25.750
Now, they are two of the
few friends I have.

03:26.580 --> 03:28.400
Happy new year.

03:28.950 --> 03:32.800
I hope that you are in good
health as spring arrives.

03:33.730 --> 03:37.650
As for myself, I have
been assigned to Mikawa.

03:38.040 --> 03:41.310
Oh, Yasuhide-sama has
been sent to Mikawa.

03:42.170 --> 03:45.760
However, I'm getting discouraged
when I think about

03:45.760 --> 03:47.620
the long, lonely trip ahead.

03:48.390 --> 03:50.370
He doesn't sound very enthusiastic.

03:51.160 --> 03:52.570
If you have some time,

03:52.570 --> 03:56.010
would you care to join
me on a tour of Mikawa?

03:56.330 --> 03:57.600
Just kidding.

03:57.600 --> 03:58.860
Here's to another great year.

04:01.180 --> 04:03.220
He always likes to joke around.

04:03.900 --> 04:09.420
Now, how should I respond
to his improper invitation?

04:09.890 --> 04:13.890
Eastward

04:09.890 --> 04:13.890
Ono no Komachi

04:26.380 --> 04:28.780
I-I took a risk by sending
out that letter.

04:28.780 --> 04:31.540
How will Komachi-dono respond?

04:31.540 --> 04:34.570
Well, she'll probably
ignore my invitation.

04:34.570 --> 04:37.310
But maybe, just maybe...

04:38.630 --> 04:43.260
She replied!

04:39.520 --> 04:41.320
She replied! Yay! Tomorrow, I get serious!

04:41.320 --> 04:42.990
Wait, this must be a trap. It starts, Yasuhide! Yes!

04:44.350 --> 04:45.130
Huh?

04:45.450 --> 04:46.950
Happy new year.

04:46.950 --> 04:48.890
Na-Narihira-dono...

04:49.890 --> 04:51.600
What happened to your hair?

04:53.450 --> 04:54.820
It's none of your business.

04:54.820 --> 04:57.090
Yes, it isn't.

04:57.540 --> 04:58.860
By the way...

04:58.860 --> 04:59.480
Huh?

05:00.310 --> 05:02.190
I heard that you're being
shipped off to Mikawa.

05:02.190 --> 05:05.210
Don't make it sound like
they're getting rid of me!

05:05.210 --> 05:06.570
Isn't that what's happening?

05:06.570 --> 05:07.920
Absolutely not!

05:07.920 --> 05:11.060
Well, whatever.  I'll be hitching
a ride for part of the way.

05:11.060 --> 05:11.620
What?

05:12.420 --> 05:15.620
I've been meaning to visit the east.

05:16.290 --> 05:19.940
You probably won't be
bringing any women along.

05:19.940 --> 05:20.650
Grr.

05:20.650 --> 05:24.690
I'll keep you company
on the long journey.

05:24.690 --> 05:26.200
You should show some gratitude.

05:27.100 --> 05:28.960
Sorry to disappoint you.

05:28.960 --> 05:29.700
Hmm?

05:29.700 --> 05:33.940
There are women who will
miss me once I'm gone!

05:33.940 --> 05:35.340
You jest.

05:35.340 --> 05:37.050
I-It's true!

05:37.050 --> 05:37.960
Excuse me.

05:37.960 --> 05:38.770
What?!

05:39.140 --> 05:42.790
Komachi-sama has sent a response.

05:44.080 --> 05:46.340
O-Oh, thank you.

05:46.340 --> 05:47.780
What's this?

05:47.780 --> 05:50.240
You haven't given up on her yet?

05:50.240 --> 05:52.780
I-It's not like that!

05:52.780 --> 05:54.720
What?!  I'm saying that...

05:54.420 --> 05:55.930
Excuse me...

05:54.720 --> 05:55.930
Watch your tongue!

05:57.080 --> 06:00.210
Let me see.
Have you gotten any closer?

06:04.280 --> 06:08.790
I lie spent, adrift like
floating seagrass.

06:09.390 --> 06:13.310
If the water beckons, I shall follow.

06:14.330 --> 06:18.020
I am fallen, with no place to go,

06:18.020 --> 06:21.200
so if someone were to offer an
invitation, I would accept.

06:23.480 --> 06:27.150
Is she saying that she'll
go along with any man?

06:27.150 --> 06:28.570
Looks like it.

06:28.570 --> 06:30.320
Well, are you happy now?

06:30.320 --> 06:33.500
Of course not!
She must be joking!

06:33.500 --> 06:35.060
Naturally.

06:35.060 --> 06:36.970
So you agree?

06:37.940 --> 06:40.510
But... would Komachi-dono

06:40.510 --> 06:43.780
use a poem to send a
message that's just a joke?

06:43.780 --> 06:45.670
Hmm, you have a point...

06:46.430 --> 06:48.760
This isn't like her.

06:49.400 --> 06:50.300
Yes.

06:54.430 --> 06:56.900
Yasuhide-sama will be
leaving for Mikawa.

06:57.790 --> 07:00.760
The friends from my youth leave me

07:01.380 --> 07:04.760
and the fear I've kept
hidden rears its ugly head.

07:06.720 --> 07:11.490
Will I be left completely alone?

07:15.110 --> 07:16.620
I used my poetry and beauty

07:17.220 --> 07:20.280
to make a name for myself in
the palace, as Ono no Komachi,

07:21.430 --> 07:28.270
but it wasn't long before my flower,
hailed as a great, proud bloom, wilted away.

07:31.950 --> 07:36.260
I was unable to give the Emperor a child,

07:37.040 --> 07:42.290
so I will spend the rest of
my life alone, forgotten.

07:44.830 --> 07:48.410
If I had accepted my dear brother...

07:50.380 --> 07:53.100
If I had a chance to relive my life,

07:53.100 --> 07:55.490
would I make a different choice?

07:56.470 --> 07:58.820
No!  That's absurd!

07:59.220 --> 08:03.540
I knew what I was getting into
when I made my choice.

08:03.540 --> 08:05.060
I have no regrets!

08:06.880 --> 08:12.010
But do I have any legacy to speak of?

08:13.010 --> 08:16.310
Have I wasted my entire life?

08:17.700 --> 08:19.090
Will I die alone

08:19.790 --> 08:24.440
with no one to remember me?

08:28.430 --> 08:29.270
I'm scared!

08:30.040 --> 08:31.360
Dear brother!

08:31.360 --> 08:33.240
What should I do, dear brother?!

08:33.240 --> 08:35.860
It wasn't supposed to be like this!

08:36.550 --> 08:39.540
I don't know the answer, dear brother!

08:39.540 --> 08:41.100
Did I make the right choice?

08:41.100 --> 08:42.580
The wrong choice?

08:43.140 --> 08:44.450
Dear brother!

08:49.180 --> 08:49.970
Yes.

08:51.550 --> 08:53.840
Your dear brother is right here.

08:53.840 --> 08:55.300
Who's there?!

08:55.960 --> 09:00.640
I long to hear your voice call...

08:57.020 --> 08:58.970
Wait!  Hold on!

08:58.970 --> 08:59.920
Who are you?!

09:00.640 --> 09:01.880
Hey!

09:01.880 --> 09:04.550
I take my eyes off you for one
second and this is what you do?!

09:05.420 --> 09:07.210
I was just saying hello.

09:07.210 --> 09:09.520
What is the matter, Yoshiko-sama?!

09:09.520 --> 09:12.360
The light!  Pass me the light!

09:14.590 --> 09:15.920
Yasuhide-sama!

09:15.920 --> 09:18.490
And... Narihira-sama?!

09:18.490 --> 09:20.080
Yes, good evening.

09:20.080 --> 09:22.190
What is the meaning of this?

09:22.190 --> 09:24.140
I can't believe you two
would do such a thing!

09:24.140 --> 09:24.870
You don't understand!

09:24.870 --> 09:27.790
We were just coming to visit you!

09:27.790 --> 09:30.330
In the middle of the night?  In secret?!

09:30.330 --> 09:31.750
Well, you see...

09:32.140 --> 09:33.610
We had our reasons...

09:35.790 --> 09:36.720
In other words,

09:36.720 --> 09:39.930
you were worried about me because of

09:39.930 --> 09:42.890
the tone of my poem,
so you came to check on me,

09:42.890 --> 09:45.030
and brought Narihira-sama,

09:45.030 --> 09:46.690
who happened to be with you.

09:47.410 --> 09:49.440
And Narihira-sama decided to
engage in some mischief.

09:50.350 --> 09:52.330
Is that correct?

09:52.330 --> 09:53.230
Yes.

09:53.590 --> 09:55.270
I appreciate your concern,

09:55.270 --> 09:56.790
but I must say that I'm disappointed.

09:56.790 --> 10:02.120
I expected you to realize that
my poem was merely a joke...

10:03.440 --> 10:05.700
Oh, Narihira-sama...

10:05.700 --> 10:06.660
Yes?

10:07.050 --> 10:09.830
Your hair is much shorter.

10:10.290 --> 10:12.080
When did you cut it?

10:12.080 --> 10:14.830
Oh, this is just cosplay.

10:14.830 --> 10:15.620
Cos...

10:15.620 --> 10:18.010
I-It's not very tidy.

10:18.440 --> 10:20.100
Seriously.

10:20.100 --> 10:22.160
What happened?

10:22.640 --> 10:26.390
Yes, it's a long story...

10:27.290 --> 10:29.260
I made a mistake
while battling a demon

10:29.260 --> 10:30.810
and my hair was eaten.

10:32.530 --> 10:33.980
Just kidding.

10:33.980 --> 10:35.280
Yes, I know.

10:35.930 --> 10:39.000
I fell in love with a princess
who was off limits,

10:39.000 --> 10:40.740
and her outraged brother
cut my hair off.

10:41.210 --> 10:43.570
What do you think you're
doing to Takaiko?!

10:42.620 --> 10:43.570
Ouch, ouch, ouch...

10:43.570 --> 10:44.730
Stop it, Brother!

10:44.270 --> 10:46.240
Ouch... Ouch...

10:44.730 --> 10:47.830
Run away, Narihira!  Run!

10:48.880 --> 10:51.190
Sounds like quite an ordeal.

10:51.690 --> 10:52.290
Yes.

10:53.010 --> 10:55.750
I can understand why you're upset,

10:56.170 --> 11:00.260
but it was immature of you to
attack me as a distraction.

11:00.820 --> 11:02.370
A distraction?

11:02.880 --> 11:05.470
I was unable to restrain my love.

11:05.990 --> 11:07.180
That's all.

11:08.600 --> 11:12.200
Oh?  And when did you
fall in love with me?

11:12.200 --> 11:14.220
The moment I first met you.

11:14.630 --> 11:17.150
I was merely using his
concern as an excuse.

11:17.740 --> 11:21.730
I intended to confess
my love to you tonight.

11:23.500 --> 11:24.860
Narihira-sama...

11:26.140 --> 11:29.270
If you need someone to
comfort you, try elsewhere!

11:29.270 --> 11:30.620
I won't be able to help.

11:32.730 --> 11:34.500
Such a heartless friend, you are.

11:36.630 --> 11:39.430
Well, enough joking around.

11:39.430 --> 11:42.050
I don't plan on falling in love again.

11:43.320 --> 11:45.320
I'm done with women.

11:45.940 --> 11:49.510
Oh, you must have truly loved her.

11:50.490 --> 11:54.020
That's why I thought I would take a
trip to the east, to soothe my heart.

11:54.810 --> 11:57.790
It just so happens that Yasuhide
is being shipped off to the boonies,

11:57.790 --> 12:00.540
so I'll accompany him to Mikawa.

12:00.540 --> 12:01.880
You're still talking about that?!

12:01.880 --> 12:04.410
When did I become your chauffeur?!

12:04.410 --> 12:05.180
You don't like that idea?

12:05.180 --> 12:06.580
Absolutely!

12:06.580 --> 12:09.860
You think I want to spend three
days listening to you rib me?!

12:09.860 --> 12:10.850
You're thrilled?

12:10.850 --> 12:12.040
I'm not thrilled!

12:13.850 --> 12:16.590
Neither of you have changed at all.

12:16.590 --> 12:19.580
This reminds me of when
we were all young.

12:21.370 --> 12:26.140
Well, the moon is just as beautiful
tonight as it was that first night.

12:27.190 --> 12:30.270
Why don't we enjoy some moon-gazing?

12:36.320 --> 12:37.910
Well, gentlemen?

12:37.910 --> 12:41.280
How do you feel after
gazing at this moon?

12:41.870 --> 12:45.550
I'm trying to come to
terms with my old age.

12:45.550 --> 12:46.940
Fancy that.

12:46.940 --> 12:48.990
I had the same reaction.

12:48.990 --> 12:51.080
Same here.

12:51.860 --> 12:55.390
So that youthful sensation
I had was merely an illusion.

12:55.960 --> 12:58.130
The moon remains unchanged,

12:58.870 --> 13:00.600
while people grow old.

13:01.790 --> 13:04.840
S-Since the moon is ruining the
mood, let's gaze at the yard.

13:04.840 --> 13:07.300
Look at the beautiful camellias.

13:07.770 --> 13:09.090
Yes...

13:09.640 --> 13:10.430
But...

13:11.250 --> 13:15.770
The wintersweet blossoms next to them have
been ravaged by the extended rains!

13:15.770 --> 13:18.900
You're making everything sound negative!

13:19.690 --> 13:21.620
Nothing wrong with that.

13:24.020 --> 13:26.160
The moon makes us lonely.

13:26.550 --> 13:28.470
The flowers make us sad.

13:29.470 --> 13:32.750
This is how people enjoy themselves
once they've gotten too old.

13:32.750 --> 13:37.060
Oh?  I thought you would never
be one to worry about your age,

13:37.060 --> 13:38.590
but look at you now.

13:38.590 --> 13:41.230
Was it difficult to have
your heart broken?

13:41.230 --> 13:42.990
Yes,

13:42.990 --> 13:46.760
though it was life, not love,
that defeated me.

13:46.760 --> 13:48.210
That sounds a little fatalistic.

13:48.210 --> 13:50.300
You still have much to look forward to.

13:50.750 --> 13:56.020
Yes, but at my age, I'm no longer
free to seek new love.

13:58.440 --> 14:03.900
I've spent my life
searching for The One,

14:04.750 --> 14:06.770
but when I found her,

14:06.770 --> 14:09.570
and she was beyond my reach,

14:10.940 --> 14:15.330
I was too old to overcome
the obstacles between us.

14:16.560 --> 14:19.700
I'm too old to wait around.

14:20.120 --> 14:22.510
I'm too old to hope for another chance.

14:23.350 --> 14:25.630
When I finally found the
answer I was seeking,

14:25.630 --> 14:28.370
I was too old to appreciate it.

14:28.370 --> 14:30.260
A sad story.

14:31.000 --> 14:32.640
Indeed...

14:32.640 --> 14:37.370
Looking back, many years
have passed fruitlessly...

14:46.290 --> 14:47.940
So the flower has wilted

14:47.940 --> 14:50.200
during the long spring rains,

14:50.860 --> 14:52.590
just as my beauty has faded

14:52.590 --> 14:54.290
during my forlorn years in this world.

14:56.690 --> 15:00.170
A pretty flower must wilt one day.

15:00.170 --> 15:05.590
After years of worrying,
I became an old woman.

15:07.770 --> 15:10.260
That poem really hurts.

15:11.490 --> 15:15.140
It resonates with me, as one who devoted
my life to the pursuit of my dream.

15:15.760 --> 15:18.710
If I'd gotten married,
perhaps by now I would be...

15:26.940 --> 15:30.290
Well, it's time to end this party.

15:30.830 --> 15:33.200
Try to visit earlier next time.

15:33.860 --> 15:36.490
We'll have more time to talk that way.

15:37.420 --> 15:39.600
Enjoy your trip to Mikawa.

15:39.600 --> 15:41.170
Don't argue too much.

15:46.780 --> 15:47.990
Komachi-dono.

15:48.920 --> 15:51.960
Would you have composed that poem

15:51.960 --> 15:54.900
if you had gotten married
and had children?

15:57.090 --> 15:59.020
Probably not.

15:59.810 --> 16:01.470
You were able to
compose that poem

16:01.470 --> 16:04.230
because you have
no place to call home,

16:06.350 --> 16:09.310
and it is a poem that
everyone can understand.

16:10.040 --> 16:13.830
Everyone has regrets of some sort.

16:14.530 --> 16:19.750
Your poem is able to reach
out to those regrets.

16:20.450 --> 16:22.580
Our poetry is where we belong.

16:23.290 --> 16:25.080
That's what you once said.

16:26.060 --> 16:26.800
Yes.

16:27.240 --> 16:29.760
Yasuhide said something very similar.

16:30.460 --> 16:34.330
I've been thinking about that recently.

16:34.980 --> 16:38.530
I've done some crazy things.

16:38.530 --> 16:41.850
Looking back, I have a lot of regrets,

16:41.850 --> 16:46.690
but I have a legacy, so it's okay.

16:47.460 --> 16:48.820
I'm assuming that you
both feel the same way.

16:50.860 --> 16:53.200
Our poems are our legacy.

16:55.080 --> 16:58.250
It doesn't have to be fame

16:58.250 --> 17:00.760
or children that you leave to this world.

17:00.760 --> 17:01.700
Exactly.

17:02.390 --> 17:04.380
We're poets,

17:04.380 --> 17:08.690
so our poetry will serve
as evidence of our lives.

17:08.690 --> 17:11.740
Endure the pain and stand tall,

17:11.740 --> 17:16.760
and keep thinking and writing poetry.

17:20.140 --> 17:21.100
Yes.

17:25.310 --> 17:27.310
So, Komachi...

17:27.310 --> 17:29.020
Come to Mikawa with us.

17:31.830 --> 17:33.010
I beg you!

17:33.010 --> 17:35.990
You were serious about
inviting me along?!

17:36.270 --> 17:38.150
No, I was joking,

17:38.150 --> 17:41.120
but I don't want to travel
alone with Narihira-dono!

17:41.670 --> 17:43.160
I feel the same way.

17:43.500 --> 17:45.810
But I've spent my whole
life in the city,

17:45.810 --> 17:47.330
so I wouldn't know what to do.

17:47.600 --> 17:50.240
Please!  As a favor to me!

17:50.240 --> 17:51.760
I beg you, Komachi-dono!

17:51.760 --> 17:53.340
Please!  Please!

17:54.310 --> 17:55.380
Honestly...

17:56.830 --> 18:00.680
My flower did not leave
any seeds behind.

18:01.320 --> 18:07.250
Instead, it will continue to
bloom in the form of my poetry.

18:08.370 --> 18:12.700
My poems give meaning to my life.

18:13.460 --> 18:16.900
Though I will surely look back many times

18:17.730 --> 18:22.580
and wonder if I would have
done anything differently,

18:23.340 --> 18:27.880
I will have my answer once I've made it

18:28.510 --> 18:31.360
through the remainder of my life.

18:35.850 --> 18:38.800
Tsurayuki and Kisen

18:35.850 --> 18:38.800
The Monk Kisen

18:37.470 --> 18:42.300
So, Yasuhide,
Komachi, and Narihira

18:42.730 --> 18:46.170
set off on a journey to the east.

18:46.170 --> 18:48.500
Oh, good Monk Kisen.

18:48.500 --> 18:50.560
I've never heard this story before.

18:51.250 --> 18:55.040
Well, I heard about the
trip from Yasuhide,

18:55.040 --> 18:57.290
so I don't know if it's true.

18:58.130 --> 18:59.200
Say, Tsurayuki.

18:59.200 --> 19:00.310
Yes?

19:00.900 --> 19:03.450
I see that you've been taking notes.

19:03.940 --> 19:07.960
Are you going to include that
episode in the preface?

19:07.960 --> 19:09.870
Huh?  Oh, no.

19:09.870 --> 19:12.760
This is a different matter.
There's talk of a literary work

19:12.760 --> 19:15.570
based on Narihira's
romantic adventures,

19:15.570 --> 19:18.410
called "The Tales of the General."

19:18.410 --> 19:21.050
Oh, the title "The Tales
of Ise" would also work.

19:21.510 --> 19:23.510
Tales?

19:24.050 --> 19:27.800
It's a new fad to write
stories in verse.

19:27.800 --> 19:31.200
This will be a work of fiction that's
modeled after Narihira's life.

19:31.200 --> 19:33.670
It's guaranteed to be
a hit with the ladies!

19:33.670 --> 19:34.940
I see...

19:34.940 --> 19:37.910
People are looking for
stories written in verse.

19:38.430 --> 19:40.680
We live in a wonderful age.

19:40.680 --> 19:41.200
Huh?

19:41.940 --> 19:45.820
The story and anthology

19:45.820 --> 19:51.170
are only possible because the
palace is now filled with poetry.

19:51.170 --> 19:55.420
When we were young,
poetry was considered a hobby,

19:55.420 --> 19:58.090
and poets were not very respected.

19:58.680 --> 20:02.000
However, Yasuhide had a
different perspective.

20:02.350 --> 20:08.060
When I first moved here,
Yasuhide came to visit me.

20:09.200 --> 20:11.570
You've chosen an interesting place to live.

20:12.520 --> 20:13.850
It can be very inconvenient.

20:14.400 --> 20:16.660
You won't have to listen
to any of that city noise.

20:16.660 --> 20:18.320
Perfect for a cynic like yourself.

20:18.560 --> 20:21.570
What?  So you also think
I'm a crazy hermit?

20:22.110 --> 20:23.400
No, I don't.

20:23.400 --> 20:25.320
Though that's what they're
all saying back in the city.

20:25.780 --> 20:28.750
I chose to live out here.

20:29.380 --> 20:33.130
The ones spreading rumors are the ones
who want to escape from the city.

20:34.940 --> 20:39.090
My own home is a retreat lying
southeast of the capital

20:39.090 --> 20:41.980
where I can hide from the
troubles of this world.

20:43.510 --> 20:46.990
I live here because it's nice and quiet,

20:46.990 --> 20:48.810
though some people would imply

20:48.810 --> 20:50.880
that I wanted to escape the city.

20:52.010 --> 20:54.990
Deep down, they envy you.

20:55.450 --> 20:58.770
They're making up rumors,
so they can feel better about

20:58.770 --> 21:00.920
staying in the city.

21:00.920 --> 21:02.500
You could always become a monk

21:02.500 --> 21:03.990
and live in the mountains.

21:04.590 --> 21:07.590
You're free to compose as
much poetry as you wish.

21:10.570 --> 21:12.220
Munesada-sama continued to

21:12.220 --> 21:15.290
write poetry after becoming a monk,

21:15.730 --> 21:20.210
but I believe that my poetry
can help me in the palace.

21:22.130 --> 21:24.980
Well, you have chosen to live here,

21:24.980 --> 21:27.600
and I have chosen to stay in the city.

21:29.060 --> 21:30.330
Now that I think about it,

21:30.330 --> 21:34.110
Yasuhide realized that, one day,

21:34.110 --> 21:36.110
poetry would bring
esteem in the palace.

21:36.110 --> 21:36.730
Yes.

21:37.070 --> 21:39.790
Well, he died before it happened,

21:39.790 --> 21:41.660
so he must be pretty upset.

21:41.660 --> 21:44.650
I could have been a great person!

21:46.870 --> 21:51.620
They were still very influential
as contemporary poets.

21:53.710 --> 21:55.100
They were responsible for

21:55.100 --> 21:58.080
bringing an age when the Emperor
commissions poetry anthologies.

21:58.080 --> 21:59.660
Their poems and hopes

21:59.660 --> 22:01.420
helped to change poetry's status.

22:01.920 --> 22:06.260
That's why I want to put
their names in the preface.

22:07.200 --> 22:09.970
I'm glad to hear you say that.

22:11.110 --> 22:13.540
The Six Poetic Geniuses lived

22:13.540 --> 22:16.640
in an age when poets were not respected,

22:16.640 --> 22:18.920
but they were driven to continue

22:18.920 --> 22:22.320
by their love of poetry
and pride in their work.

22:23.620 --> 22:27.930
They made their poetry their legacy.

22:28.470 --> 22:29.280
Yeah?

22:29.450 --> 22:31.470
Isn't that right, Tsurayuki-senpai?

22:31.470 --> 22:32.540
Yep.

22:32.990 --> 22:34.990
Poetic Tale 5:

22:32.990 --> 22:34.990
END

24:05.000 --> 24:20.880
Next
Episode

24:05.000 --> 24:20.880
Uta Hen+

24:05.000 --> 24:20.880
Plus

24:07.020 --> 24:16.990
In the sleepy spring sunlight,
pink, pink sha-la-la.
